cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FlahaX, please cite it as below."
title: "FlahaX: plant-nutrient chemistry engine for fertilizer formulation and delivery planning"
abstract: >-
  FlahaX is a Python package for plant nutrition. It chooses fertilizer salts
  and grams so that a fixed crop formula, after subtraction of the source
  water, is met; models the resulting solution with fertilizer-specific
  aqueous equilibrium chemistry (speciation, precipitation and pH); plans the
  acid dose to a target pH; and plans stock tanks and injection with
  auditable units, model identifiers and source hashes. Chemistry results are
  verified against PHREEQC.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Al Khashan
    given-names: Rafat A.
version: 0.3.1
url: https://pypi.org/project/flahax/
repository-code: https://github.com/rafatahmed/Flahax
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - fertilizer
  - hydroponics
  - nutrient solution
  - formulation
  - non-negative least squares
  - fertigation
  - aqueous equilibrium
  - plant nutrition
